0 Three loops of studded chain wrap around coarse-toothed wheels of very different sizes.
0 Name: TECHNIC_CHAIN_LINK_WITH_TWO_STUDS-Constraints.ldr
0 Author: J.C. Tchang
0 Unofficial Model
0 // Scene: Black links form a small low loop, a taller angled loop and a broad loop dominated by one large wheel. The studs on the outward faces suggest attachment points for carried pieces.
0 // Rigid construction: This is the older large-tooth gear family: 569, 570, 641, 642, 644 and 741. Their wheel geometry is distinct from the modern small Technic gear examples.
0 // Build lesson: Studded links offer a visual starting point for moving trays, buckets or conveyor flights; design those attachments around the actual link and wheel family.
0 // Reuse: The wheels have no complete bearing frame here. Studs do not make the links interchangeable with another chain or track system; add support, retention and clearance studies.
0 // Study 1: The first loop compares a small and a very large coarse-toothed wheel.
0 SYNTH BEGIN TECHNIC_CHAIN_LINK_WITH_TWO_STUDS 0
0 SYNTH SHOW
0 ROTATION CENTER 0 0 0 1 "Custom" 
0 ROTATION CONFIG 0 1
0 // Technic Gear  9 Large Tooth (trans_clear)
1 47 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 569.DAT
0 // Technic Gear 21 Large Tooth (trans_clear)
1 47 80 152 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 642.dat
0 // Technic Gear 42 Large Tooth (trans_clear)
1 47 230 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 644.dat
0 SYNTH END
0 // Study 2: The second loop makes a taller arrangement around another gear pairing.
